We want school meals in England to: 

• contain no added sugar and provide no sugary drinks, while allowing naturally occurring sugars in whole fruit, vegetables and milk; 
• exclude routine cakes, ice cream and sweetened desserts; 
• include more vegetables, fruit, pulses and wholegrains; 
• contain less salt and saturated fat and fewer highly processed foods;
• have stronger monitoring and enforcement to ensure standards are followed.

The aim is to help children develop healthy eating habits for life
